<!--
Types which only the instance nodes reach (opcua/instance-coverage).
- AlphaType declares a mandatory child "Blocks" of FolderType. The declaration adds, with HasAddIn, a child "State"
  of BetaType (the building blocks pattern of OPC 40001-1). FolderType defines no members, so the walk along the
  type definitions never reaches BetaType; the instance contains a BetaType entity all the same.
- BetaType defines a mandatory variable "Level" and an optional "Note". The instance's State has a Note but lacks
  Level: validation has to report it.
- AlphaType declares a mandatory child "Delta" of DeltaType; the instance uses DeltaSubType, which defines no member
  of its own and stays covered by DeltaType's shape.
- The instance's Blocks carries a variable "Extra" which neither a type nor a declaration defines.
-->

